cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this work, please cite the methodology and the label-only gold
  standard. A full BibTeX entry is provided in CITATION.bib.
title: >-
  Can a Model Judge Whether a Task Is Done? A Negative-Result Study on
  Obligation-Closure Judgment
abstract: >-
  We attempted to build a classifier that judges whether a user obligation is
  closed by an agent's utterance. Five modeling families were tested and
  excluded with causal experiments; at adequate statistical power the
  obligation-aware model is indistinguishable from a zero-semantic baseline,
  and a same-ruler comparison shows a 287M fine-tuned model and a large
  general LLM perform within 2.5pp. We argue the failure is a task-definition
  problem, not a modeling one.
keywords:
  - agent observability
  - obligation closure
  - negative result
  - evaluation methodology
  - gliner
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
